type: software
title: "From Hahn to Twirling in 60 Seconds"
abstract: >-
  A short explainer, a perspective with an experimental proposal, and a
  reproducible finite-pulse Bloch-vector simulation that contrast Hahn-echo
  refocusing with an {I, X} channel twirl in a Ramsey sequence on the clock
  transition of a single 25Mg+ ion. For a static detuning the echo rephases the
  spin, the pooled twirl shows a contrast zero and a phase-reversed revival,
  and conditioning on the recorded frame bit recovers opposite fringes at the
  pooled zero. All numbers are model predictions with illustrative parameters;
  the repository contains no measured data.
